### Recorrido de un comando

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
{{#if hasWebApi}}
    participant C as Cliente HTTP
    participant E as {{Entity}}Endpoints
{{/if}}
{{#unless hasWebApi}}
    participant C as Navegador
    participant E as {{EntityPlural}}.razor
{{/unless}}
    participant D as IDispatcher
    participant B as Pipeline<br/>logging + validación
    participant H as Register{{Entity}}Handler
    participant A as {{Entity}} (agregado)
    participant U as IUnitOfWork
    participant P as Manejadores de eventos

{{#if hasWebApi}}
    C->>E: POST /api/{{entityRoute}}
{{/if}}
{{#unless hasWebApi}}
    C->>E: alta desde /{{entityRoute}}
{{/unless}}
    E->>D: SendAsync(Register{{Entity}}Command)
    D->>B: envuelve el handler
    B->>B: valida forma del comando
    B->>H: HandleAsync(command)
    H->>A: {{Entity}}.Register(...)
    Note over A: valida invariantes<br/>y registra {{Entity}}RegisteredDomainEvent
    H->>U: SaveChangesAsync()
    U->>P: publica los eventos acumulados
    H-->>E: Result&lt;{{Entity}}Response&gt;
    E-->>C: 201 Created / 400 / 409
```

La presentación no conoce `Register{{Entity}}Handler`. Sólo construye un mensaje y lo despacha:
por eso **añadir un caso de uso no obliga a tocar la capa web**.

